      "text": "News\n\nCasualties\n\nKurdish forces/ SDF\n\nMrs. Fatoum Ghazi al Lour, from Aleppo governorate, died in Mreimein village of Afrin city in the northern suburbs of Aleppo on January 20, 2022, when Syrian Democratic Forces personnel targeted the civilian vehicle she was in with a missile.\nSNHR confirms that, through this attack, the Syrian Democratic Forces have undeniably violated UN Security Council Resolutions 2139 and 2254 that prohibit arbitrary attacks, as well as willfully disregarding international humanitarian law regarding the distinction between civilians and combatants.\n\nThe daily death toll of civilian victims in Syria on February 7, 2022\n\nA girl was killed by the explosion of a mine left by an unknown party, southwest of Hasaka on February 6\n\nThe daily death toll of civilian victims in Syria on February 6, 2022\n\nSyrian Democratic Forces arrested two reporters northeast of Hasaka governorate on February 5\n\nNational Syrian Army arrested a woman north of Aleppo governorate on February 2\n\nA solidarity rally by residents of the Kyangwali Refugee Settlement in Uganda in support of the forcibly disappeared case in Syria"
    }
  ],
